{"profile":{"name":"Jamaal Myers","ward":"Ward 23, Scarborough North","bio":"Jamaal Myers was first elected to Toronto City Council on October 24, 2022 and took office November 15, 2022, filling the Ward 23 seat after the sudden death of incumbent Cynthia Lai days before the election. Before entering politics he worked as a corporate lawyer, most recently as senior legal counsel at TD Bank focusing on environmental, social and governance matters. Born and raised in Scarborough in Toronto Community Housing, he holds a BA from the University of Western Ontario, an MSc from the London School of Economics, and a JD from New York University.","committees":["Toronto Transit Commission Board (Chair)","Toronto Accessibility Advisory Committee (Chair)","Planning and Housing Committee","Audit Committee","Scarborough Community Council"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_myers@toronto.ca","phone":"416-338-2858"},"promises":[{"text":"Legalize and regulate rooming houses and work toward building 40,000 affordable rental homes in Toronto by 2030.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Oppose TTC service cuts, support bus lanes in Scarborough to help with traffic, and lower TTC fares.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Make the TTC free for seniors and students, and allow free transfers between TTC buses and GO Transit in Scarborough following the Scarborough LRT closure.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":311,"term":311,"first":"2022-11-17","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":83,"clients":77,"subjects":147,"methods":{"Meetings":107,"Emails":162,"Phone calls":24,"Written":7,"Other or unreported":11},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":75},{"label":"Transportation","count":60},{"label":"Transit / TTC","count":57},{"label":"By-law / Regulation","count":47},{"label":"Planning and Development","count":31}],"years":[{"year":2022,"count":14},{"year